<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 13:30:31 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Amid France’s political 'fragmentation', 'a case needs to be made for participatory democracy’</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/amid-france-s-political-fragmentation-a-case-needs-to-be-made-for-participatory-democracy</link><description>
Carys Garland is pleased to welcome Dr. Andrew Smith, Historian of Modern France and Lecturer in Liberal Arts at Queen Mary University of London. He argues that Marine Le Pen and the National Rally’s commanding position in early presidential polling should not be regarded as an inevitable far-right victory. They are benefiting from familiarity, unity and laser-focused messaging. More fundamentally, however, Smith sees the polling as a reflection of a French electorate shaped by anger, anxiety, economic insecurity and political fatigue. Rather than describing this landscape simply as one of growing “polarization,” he proposes the more revealing concept of “fragmentation.” 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3b0a1158-b0bc-11f1-bc3a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-151821-152731-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3b0a1158-b0bc-11f1-bc3a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-151821-152731-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">40a0aea6-b0bc-11f1-a3f6-8d5ebd0252fb</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 08:01:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Corruption ‘endemic’ in Trump administration: 'Checks and balances only in effect at lower courts'</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260915-corruption-endemic-in-trump-administration-checks-and-balances-only-in-effect-at-lower-courts</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Andrew Weissmann, Author, Professor at NYU School of Law, and former General Counsel of the FBI. He argues that as political deception and deliberate falsehoods become normalized, and politically useful, it erodes any trust we have in our government and our institutions. Drawing on his book, "Liar’s Kingdom", Weissmann questions why political leaders are above the law in the United States, while ordinary citizens risk serious legal consequences for making intentionally false statements.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/134880ea-b0b3-11f1-871a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-180947-182810-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/134880ea-b0b3-11f1-871a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-180947-182810-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">74a4dd9e-b0da-11f1-9bd1-b95f3054049f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 07:52:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lack of 'enforcement of EU laws': Consumer products contain 'illegal levels of restricted chemicals'</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/lack-of-enforcement-of-eu-laws-consumer-products-contain-illegal-levels-of-restricted-chemicals</link><description>
Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Hélène Duguy, Senior Environmental Lawyer at ClientEarth. PFAS pollution is widespread, these highly persistent chemicals have been detected in water and soil, food and consumer products, and even the human body. The risks are increasingly well documented, alternatives now exist for many uses, and there is an extensive regulatory framework that is in place. Duguy argues that the central problem is therefore not simply a lack of scientific knowledge or legislation, but rather weak enforcement, slow regulation and corporate resistance. And so hazardous chemicals remain in circulation even when restrictions exist. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6221f4c0-b0c3-11f1-b095-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-081030-081732-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6221f4c0-b0c3-11f1-b095-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-081030-081732-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">675edb1a-b0c3-11f1-a424-7561ae3caee9</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 07:28:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French labour strike reduces capacity at key Dunkirk gas terminal</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/france/20260915-french-labour-strike-reduces-capacity-key-dunkirk-gas-terminal</link><description>
Industrial action ​was expected to reduce French electricity supply by up to 5 gigawatts on ⁠Tuesday as energy sector ⁠unions stage a 24-hour strike in protest over calls to curb ​employee benefits ‌such as access to cheaper power.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dcb46572-b0d4-11f1-a26a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par8222043.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dcb46572-b0d4-11f1-a26a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par8222043.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">448af400-b0d4-11f1-9ea0-cdc1ec495daa</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 07:24:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dcb46572-b0d4-11f1-a26a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par8222043.jpg">© Denis Charlet, AFP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Iran war exposes US munitions shortfall, industrial bottlenecks, Pentagon report says</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-iran-war-exposes-us-munitions-shortfall-industrial-bottlenecks-pentagon-report-says</link><description>
